OL,3,GNEWSA'Being part of Homeless World Cup
OL,4,Awas life-changing'
OL,5,
OL,6,FFootballers across the north of England
OL,7,Fhave been given the chance to represent
OL,8,Ftheir country in next year's Homeless
OL,9,FWorld Cup in Mexico.
OL,11,FTrials for the men's England team have
OL,12,Ftaken place in Middlesbrough, where
OL,13,Fplayers from Teesside, Newcastle and
OL,14,FLiverpool tried to impress the watching
OL,15,Fscouts.
OL,17,FTo qualify for selection, players have
OL,18,Fto have recently experienced
OL,19,Fhomelessness, have refugee status, or
OL,20,Fbe in a drug rehabilitation scheme.
OL,23,APub: 04-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
